# debug-shell's workload is its own full pod name (debug-shell-aws/-gce),
# not a shared "debug-shell" - unlike the controller-owned workloads above
# (a Deployment/DaemonSet/etc. genuinely has one name shared across
# clusters), a bare pod has no controller identity to unify around, and its
# kube_pod_owner{owner_kind=""} row (below) independently derives "workload"
# from the pod's own name via label_replace - matching that here (rather
# than the earlier "debug-shell" shorthand) keeps both metrics in agreement.
# They used to disagree (this row said "debug-shell", kube_pod_owner-derived
# rows said "debug-shell-aws"/"-gce"), which (a) silently split the
# Workloads page's debug-shell entry into two partial rows after `merge`
